  "Id": 2464,
  "Title": "ISMC holds convocation ceremony",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations third convocation celebrated.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass6C13ADF4CE134060A40EE27AC4A78CF6\"><p>Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations&#160;held its third convocation on February 12, 2011 at School of Oriental and African Studies, University College of London, where 18 graduates received their MA in Muslim Cultures.&#160;</p><p>The chief guest was Professor Richard Pring,&#160;Lead Director of the Nuffield Review of 14-19 education and training and the former Director of the Department of Educational Studies at Oxford University.&#160;</p><p>The ceremony was attended by senior officials of AKU, faculty and staff, as well as invited guests from the academic, government and diplomatic communities in London.\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br></p></div>",
